Port: find helpers, the injected bundle and GIO plugins next to the engine.

Upstream compiles the install prefix into the library: the helper
executables, the injected bundle and (in GLib) the GIO module directory are
looked up at absolute paths, so a build only runs from where it was
installed. When ZEBKIT_RELOCATABLE is defined
(profiles/include/size-prelude.h), the engine asks the dynamic loader where
libWPEWebKit itself was loaded from and looks there first:

    <engine dir>/WPEWebProcess, WPENetworkProcess
    <engine dir>/libWPEInjectedBundle.so
    <engine dir>/gio/modules/          (added to GIO_EXTRA_MODULES)

Anything not found there falls back to the compiled-in path, so an ordinary
installed build keeps working. Without the define, behaviour is unchanged.

